language 0.1.0
module security
  means
    Protection of valuable entities from threats by means of policies,
    controls and explicitly established boundaries of trust.

entity asset : thing
  means
    asset: an entity holding value and requiring protection.

entity threat : thing
  means
    threat: a potential cause of unwanted impact upon an asset.

entity vulnerability : thing
  means
    vulnerability: a property of a system that a threat can use to break a
    security property.

entity control : thing
  means
    control: a technical or organisational means of reducing a security risk.

entity policy : thing
  means
    policy: a normative set of rules for admissible handling of assets.

entity trust-boundary : thing
  means
    trust boundary: a boundary between areas holding different assumptions
    about trust and control.

entity security-property : thing
  means
    security property: a verifiable characteristic of the protection of an
    asset or a system.
